            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>Problem: Running Out of Balance Is Not a Minor Issue</h2>
<p>In overseas ad campaigns, running out of account balance often happens at critical moments—before major sales events, during new creative testing, or when you need to outbid competitors. One cross-border e-commerce team lost about 15% of potential orders when their ads paused for 2 hours on Prime Day due to insufficient balance.</p>
<p>Balance alerts seem like basic configuration, but in practice, alert failures, recharge delays, and payment restrictions frequently occur. This checklist helps teams systematically identify potential issues.</p>
<h2>Checklist Item 1: Are Alert Thresholds Reasonable?</h2>
<p><strong>Operational requirement:</strong> Alert thresholds should cover the entire time from alert to recharge completion.</p>
<ul>
<li>For accounts spending $500/day, recharge typically takes 1-4 hours to process</li>
<li>Set two-level alerts: notify operations when balance drops to 1x daily spend, notify finance at 0.5x</li>
<li>Verify that alerts are configured for each account individually, not relying on platform defaults</li>
<li>Ensure notifications reach the responsible person, not just the admin account</li>
</ul>
<h2>Checklist Item 2: Are Recharge Channels Unblocked?</h2>
<p><strong>Operational requirement:</strong> Both primary and backup payment methods should be available.</p>
<ul>
<li>Confirm the daily limit of primary payment method (credit card/business transfer) meets your needs</li>
<li>Check for any payment failures due to account restrictions</li>
<li>Prepare at least 2 payment methods as backup: PayPal, corporate Alipay, bank transfer</li>
<li>Test with a small amount first to confirm the channel works</li>
</ul>
<h2>Checklist Item 3: Is Balance Balanced Across Multiple Accounts?</h2>
<p><strong>Operational requirement:</strong> Balance across multiple ad accounts should be under unified monitoring.</p>
<ul>
<li>When managing more than 3 accounts, use the management dashboard's balance monitoring feature</li>
<li>High-volume accounts are harder to predict; prioritize monitoring main campaigns</li>
<li>Separate test accounts from production accounts to prevent testing from affecting key campaigns</li>
<li>Establish daily balance reporting; verify all account balances before market open</li>
</ul>
<h2>Checklist Item 4: Is Auto-Recharge Enabled?</h2>
<p><strong>Operational requirement:</strong> Evaluate enabling auto-recharge on supported platforms.</p>
<ul>
<li>Google Ads and Meta Business Manager both offer auto-recharge options</li>
<li>Set trigger thresholds but also set maximum limits to prevent overcharges</li>
<li>Auto-recharge should supplement, not replace, manual monitoring</li>
<li>Verify the payment method is long-term valid to avoid failures from expired cards</li>
</ul>
<h2>Checklist Item 5: Are Emergency Contacts in Place?</h2>
<p><strong>Operational requirement:</strong> When balance runs out outside business hours, have an emergency response mechanism.</p>
<ul>
<li>Ensure finance or account admin can be reached outside working hours</li>
<li>Establish a balance alert group including media buying, operations, and finance</li>
<li>Define emergency recharge authorization process to avoid delays from approval chains</li>
<li>For important campaign dates, complete recharge 24 hours in advance</li>
</ul>
<h2>Quick Self-Check List</h2>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Alert thresholds cover recharge processing time</li>
<li>[ ] Both primary and backup payment methods tested</li>
<li>[ ] Multi-account balance under unified monitoring</li>
<li>[ ] Auto-recharge evaluated and decision confirmed</li>
<li>[ ] Emergency contact list updated</li>
<li>[ ] Balance verified 24 hours before important dates</li>
</ul>
<h2>Closing</h2>
<p>Balance alerts are not a one-time configuration. Review alert settings monthly and adjust thresholds as campaign scale changes. Payment channels and emergency contacts should be part of new employee onboarding to avoid gaps during staff changes.</p>
<p>Building a comprehensive balance protection system is fundamental to campaign stability and reflects your team's professionalism.</p>
